# STATION 10: format extras: [a|b] text variation, <<random>> blocks, once-options,
# "cond ? a : b" inline conditions, <<wait>>, and include: of a shared file.
npc: @test_format
title: Station 10 - Format extras
speaker: Tester
include: _shared

== start
<<set $visits = $visits + 1>>
TEST 10: Format extras. [Greetings|Hello|Well met], {player}. This is visit {$visits}: {$visits > 1 ? "you have been here before" : "your first time"}. Expected: the greeting word varies between visits; the part after the colon changes after the first visit.
<<random>>
  Random block picked alternative ONE. Expected: one of three alternatives, a different one most times.
<<or>>
  Random block picked alternative TWO. Expected: one of three alternatives, a different one most times.
<<or>>
  Random block picked alternative THREE. Expected: one of three alternatives, a different one most times.
<<endrandom>>
-> Ask about the once-only secret (expect this button to vanish for good after you pick it; /lowtalk reset brings it back) <<once>>
    The secret is that this button hides itself. Look at the menu: it is gone.
    <<jump start>>
-> Test a two second pause (expect a line with no Continue button, then the next line appears by itself) <<if true>>
    Counting... one...
    <<wait 2>>
    ...two. The pause is over. Expected: about two seconds between the lines with no button press.
    <<jump start>>
-> Say the included goodbye (expect a line from the shared file _shared.talk, then Leave closes the window)
    <<jump shared_goodbye>>
-> Leave
    <<end>>
